;; The known disagreements of the per-form differential check (bin/diffcheck,
;; doc/FUTAMURA-SURVEY.md, "F2 as built"): it passes when the disagreeing cases are
;; exactly these. Rewritten by bin/diffcheck --write-expected, which keeps the reasons
;; of the cases still disagreeing; edit the reasons by hand.
{:impl "bin/diffcheck"
 :about "Clojure's pair: a corpus evaluated (the evaluator) against compiled (arbace.c2j, j2g). The Java forms' pair: interpreted (arbace.classes.interp) against translated (j2g). Found on 2026-10-17 besides these, and fixed in arbace.c2j.emit: import's value (nil compiled, the class evaluated and on the JVM: 21 cases, definterface's among them) and a deftype in a fn's code (its methods' this emitted as the fn's self: every compiled defrecord failed j2g's analysis)."
 :mismatches
 [{:reason "Clojure's pair, a real divergence of j2g: an interface method a deftype, record or reify leaves unimplemented throws UnsupportedOperationException (\"j2g: not translated: abstract ...\", j2g's stub for a method without a body) in compiled code, where the evaluator's class (and the JVM) throws AbstractMethodError. Proposal F2.3"
   :cases
   [{:case "test/oracle/forms/polymorphism.ae:462" :form "((Fn2.) 1)"}
    {:case "test/oracle/forms/polymorphism.ae:496" :form "(let [o (reify Shape (area2 [_] 9))] (scale o 2))"}
    {:case "test/oracle/forms/types.ae:33" :form "(.twice (Partial.) 1)"}
    {:case "test/oracle/forms/types.ae:294" :form "(f1 1 2 3)"}
    {:case "test/oracle/forms/types.ae:394" :form "(let [o (reify arbace.lang.IFn (invoke [_] :none))] (o 1))"}]}

  {:reason "Clojure's pair, compilation's semantics, as the JVM's AOT: compiled code makes the vars it names when its constants are made, when the namespace's loader starts (Compiler$AOT/pool), so fresh.ns/fv and scratch.space/in-scratch are interned before the cases that intern or define them run, and user/map, which a later (def map 1) defines, replaces arbace.core/map's mapping in user before (resolve 'map); evaluated code interns a var when the form naming it is analyzed"
   :cases
   [{:case "test/oracle/forms/state_errors.ae:453" :form "(count (ns-publics 'fresh.ns))"}
    {:case "test/oracle/forms/state_errors.ae:454" :form "(count (ns-map 'fresh.ns))"}
    {:case "test/oracle/forms/state_errors.ae:470" :form "(arbace.core/count (arbace.core/ns-publics 'scratch.space))"}
    {:case "test/oracle/forms/state_errors.ae:480" :form "(resolve 'map)"}]}

  {:reason "Clojure's pair, not reproducible: an identity hash (StringBuilder's), different in each run (the oracle's known mismatch of the same case)"
   :cases
   [{:case "test/oracle/forms/strings.ae:408" :form "(hash (StringBuilder. \"x\"))"}]}

  {:reason "Clojure's pair, a position in a message: eval at run time of a form without positions reports Compiler/LINE and COLUMN, which Compiler.load sets for each top-level form of an evaluated namespace but a compiled loader does not (Compiler$AOT/load, as the JVM's __init class), so the compiled run names the position of the form that loaded the namespace (the harness's, 1:33)"
   :cases
   [{:case "test/oracle/forms/harvest/vars.ae:5" :form "(eval (arbace.core/seq (arbace.core/concat (arbace.core/list (quote binding)) (arbace.core/list (arb..."}]}

  {:reason "The Java forms' pair, a limit of j2g: Clojure data in a class body (the keyword :k of ex-info's data in Ex's static initializer, the var #'arbace.core/map in Holder's) is a constant j2g does not make in a class of the program (UnsupportedOperationException \"j2g: Clojure constant ...\" when the class is initialized); the interpreter hands the body to the evaluator. The runtime's Java forms hold no Clojure constants. Proposal F2.4"
   :cases
   [{:case "test/oracle/forms/defclass.ae:427" :form "(try (Ex/npe nil) (catch NullPointerException e :npe))"}
    {:case "test/oracle/forms/defclass.ae:428" :form "(try (Ex/cce 1) (catch ClassCastException e :cce))"}
    {:case "test/oracle/forms/defclass.ae:429" :form "(try (Ex/thrower 0) (catch IllegalArgumentException e (ex-message e)))"}
    {:case "test/oracle/forms/defclass.ae:430" :form "(try (Ex/thrower 1) (catch Exception e [(ex-message e) (ex-data e)]))"}
    {:case "test/oracle/forms/defclass.ae:431" :form "(Ex/thrower 2)"}
    {:case "test/oracle/forms/defclass.ae:432" :form "(Ex/deep 1000)"}
    {:case "test/oracle/forms/native.ae:227" :form "[(Holder/twice [1 2]) (Holder/pick :b) (Holder/evens 4)]"}]}

  {:reason "The Java forms' pair, a real divergence of j2g's member tables: reflection finds no constructor of the abstract class Base translated by j2g (\"No matching ctor found\" when (Base.) is analyzed), where the interpreted class has its constructor and the call fails as on the JVM, with InstantiationError"
   :cases
   [{:case "test/oracle/forms/defclass.ae:304" :form "(try (Base.) (catch Throwable e (class e)))"}]}

  {:reason "The Java forms' pair, the interpreter's known limits (test/j2g/record_fixtures.ae: the fixtures are recorded on the JVM because of them): a class of Java forms made at run time cannot extend java.io.StringReader (FxCode) nor reach java.lang.invoke's MethodHandles (FxVarHandles); j2g translates both. The fixtures' calls of the classes the interpreter could not define then reach the compiled classes in both runs, and agree"
   :cases
   [{:case "test/j2g/fixtures:2" :form "(load-file \"test/j2g/fixtures/FxCode.ae\")"}
    {:case "test/j2g/fixtures:7" :form "(load-file \"test/j2g/fixtures/FxVarHandles.ae\")"}]}

  {:reason "The Java forms' pair, a real divergence of the interpreter: a lambda of an interface made at run time (FxPredicate) lacks the interface's default method, (.negate p) throws AbstractMethodError (j2g.fixtures.FxOuter$$Lambda/N.negate()), where j2g's lambda has it and the JVM's too. Proposal F2.5"
   :cases
   [{:case "test/j2g/fixtures:13" :form "(j2g.fixtures.FxOuter/tLambdas)"}]}

  {:reason "Clojure's pair, a real divergence of the compiled constants (SA155): a class's symbols without metadata are made once in its constant pool and named by the constants that hold them, so two equal quoted symbols of compiled code are identical; the evaluator and the JVM make one symbol per constant (Clojure leaves symbols' identity unspecified). Found once the corpora's user stayed user (the namespace dcf.user, made bare by in-ns, had no identical?). Proposal F3.3"
   :cases
